orded in `patchedDependencies`. |"," | `(<peer>)` | One group for each peer dependency that the package or its dependencies resolved from outside the package. See [peer suffixes](#peer-suffixes). |"," ","+When a `file:` directory name ends in a parenthesis, its key includes a trailing","+slash, as in `example-kit@file:vendor/(kit)/`.","+"," The keys of `packages` are the same keys without the patch hash and the peer"," suffixes. To find the `packages` entry of a snapshot, strip the trailing"," parenthesized groups. Older lockfiles can also have a","@@ -255,6 +258,8 @@ pnpm sorts the group contents and joins them with `)(`. This body includes any"," nested parentheses and excludes the outermost pair. If its UTF-8 byte length"," exceeds [`peersSuffixMaxLength`](./settings/store.md#peerssuffixmaxlength), pnpm"," replaces the body with the first 32 hex characters of its SHA-256 digest.","+If a provider's `file:` path contains parentheses, pnpm hashes the sorted","+groups with a NUL byte before each group to preserve their boundaries."," pnpm wraps the resulting body in parentheses. Use the dependency maps to"," follow resolved edges, including when a peer group is shortened or hashed."," ",""],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":149,"deletions":41,"truncated":false,"file_count":15},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-25T18:23:56.232789+00:00"}